{"units": [{"id": "krektos-word2", "translation": "woven together with wailers"}, {"id": "krektos-word3", "translation": "we shall release a strain for the city"}, {"id": "krektos-word4", "translation": "θρεκτοῖσι νόμοις [with woven strains] instead of τροχαίοις [trochaic], Sophocles in Odysseus Mad; but some read κρεκτοῖς [woven]"}, {"id": "kremas-orth1", "translation": "hanging"}, {"id": "kremas-def1", "translation": "hanging"}, {"id": "kremas-note1", "translation": "Hermann corrected the false accent in M, κρέμας γυπίας [hanging vulture's rock]."}, {"id": "kremas-quote1", "translation": "solitary-minded, hanging on the vulture's rock"}, {"id": "kremas-word1", "translation": "hanging vulture's rock"}, {"id": "kremastos-orth1", "translation": "hung up, suspended"}, {"id": "kremastos-def1", "translation": "hung up, suspended"}, {"id": "kremastos-note1", "translation": "Thus Hermann for κρεμάσασα τόξον [having hung the bow], which is in the scholium on Homer, Od. 14, 12; κρεμάσας τόξον [having hung the bow] in Eustathius p. 1748, 57."}, {"id": "kremastos-quote1", "translation": "bows hung from a dark-leaved pine"}, {"id": "kremastos-word1", "translation": "having hung the bow"}, {"id": "kremastos-word2", "translation": "having hung the bow"}, {"id": "kreoboros-orth1", "translation": "flesh-eating"}, {"id": "kreoboros-def1", "translation": "flesh-eating"}, {"id": "kreoboros-quote1", "translation": "the unwomanly flesh-eating (thus Butler's anonymous scholar for κρεοβρότους [flesh-devouring], which could also be κρεοβότους [flesh-grazing]) Amazons"}, {"id": "kreokopeo-orth1", "translation": "to cut up meat, to mangle"}, {"id": "kreokopeo-def1", "translation": "to cut up meat, to mangle"}, {"id": "kreokopeo-note1", "translation": "Another example of this verb is in Euripides, Cycl. 358 κρεοκοπεῖν μέλη ξένων [to cut up the limbs of strangers]."}, {"id": "kreokopeo-quote1", "translation": "they cut up the limbs of the wretched"}, {"id": "kreokopeo-word1", "translation": "to cut up the limbs of strangers"}, {"id": "kreourgos-orth1", "translation": "butcher, one who cuts meat"}, {"id": "kreourgos-def1", "translation": "butcher, one who cuts meat"}, {"id": "kreourgos-note1", "translation": "a feast day, on which meats are distributed to the guests."}, {"id": "kreourgos-quote1", "translation": "thinking to pass a day of feasting cheerfully"}, {"id": "kreon-orth1", "translation": "Creon"}, {"id": "kreon-def1", "translation": "Creon, son of Menoeceus, king of Thebes"}, {"id": "kreon-quote1", "translation": "Megareus, seed of Creon"}, {"id": "kreon_imperans-orth1", "translation": "ruling, lord"}, {"id": "kreon_imperans-def1", "translation": "ruling, lord"}, {"id": "kreon_imperans-quote1", "translation": "Zeus, ruling through unending time"}, {"id": "kremnamai-orth1", "translation": "to hang, be suspended"}, {"id": "kremnamai-def1", "translation": "to hang, be suspended"}, {"id": "kremnamai-quote1", "translation": "above the eyes, hanging clouds"}, {"id": "krenaios-orth1", "translation": "of a spring, fountain-"}, {"id": "krenaios-def1", "translation": "of a spring, fountain-"}, {"id": "krenaios-quote1", "translation": "around the spring's water"}, {"id": "krene-orth1", "translation": "spring, fountain"}, {"id": "krene-def1", "translation": "spring, fountain"}, {"id": "krene-note1", "translation": "Thus Canter for Λέρνης ἄκρην τε [and the height of Lerna]."}, {"id": "krene-quote1", "translation": "and the spring of Lerna"}, {"id": "krene-word1", "translation": "and the height of Lerna"}, {"id": "krenias-orth1", "translation": "of a spring, fountain-"}, {"id": "krenias-def1", "translation": "of a spring, fountain-"}, {"id": "krenias-note1", "translation": "Thus Meineke for κρήναισιν [with springs], for which also κρηναίαις [of springs] can be written."}, {"id": "krenias-quote1", "translation": "to the nymphs of the springs"}, {"id": "krenias-word1", "translation": "with springs"}, {"id": "krenias-word2", "translation": "of springs"}, {"id": "krepis-orth1", "translation": "foundation, base"}, {"id": "krepis-def1", "translation": "foundation, base"}, {"id": "krepis-quote1", "translation": "and not yet is there a foundation of evils"}, {"id": "kres-orth1", "translation": "Cretan"}, {"id": "kres-def1", "translation": "Cretan"}, {"id": "kres-quote1", "translation": "I am by birth a Cretan of most ancient lineage"}, {"id": "kressai-orth1", "translation": "Cretan Women"}, {"id": "kressai-def1", "translation": "was the title of a play by Aeschylus"}, {"id": "kretikos-orth1", "translation": "Cretan"}, {"id": "kretikos-def1", "translation": "Cretan"}, {"id": "kretikos-quote1", "translation": "with Cretan necklaces wrought of gold"}, {"id": "kribanos-orth1", "translation": "oven, pan"}, {"id": "kribanos-def1", "translation": "oven, pan"}, {"id": "kribanos-note1", "translation": "Thus I corrected what is read in Athenaeus 9 p. 375d as νοθοῦντι [spurious]."}, {"id": "kribanos-quote1", "translation": "I will place this in a roaring oven"}, {"id": "kribanos-word1", "translation": "spurious"}, {"id": "krithao-orth1", "translation": "to be wanton, to neigh"}, {"id": "krithao-def1", "translation": "to be wanton, to neigh"}, {"id": "krithao-quote1", "translation": "a colt neighing"}, {"id": "krithe-orth1", "translation": "barley"}, {"id": "krithe-def1", "translation": "barley"}, {"id": "krithe-quote1", "translation": "not drinking strong drink made from barley"}, {"id": "krima-orth1", "translation": "judgment, decision"}, {"id": "krima-def1", "translation": "judgment, decision"}, {"id": "krima-quote1", "translation": "the judgment is not easy to decide"}, {"id": "krino-orth1", "translation": "to separate, choose; to prefer; to decide, judge"}, {"id": "krino-def1", "translation": "to separate, choose"}, {"id": "krino-def2", "translation": "to prefer"}, {"id": "krino-def3", "translation": "to decide, judge"}, {"id": "krino-note1", "translation": "about interpreting dreams."}, {"id": "krino-quote1", "translation": "having chosen the best of my citizens"}, {"id": "krino-quote2", "translation": "and from it the tawny horse-cock | drips much toil of chosen drugs (thus Hermann for κηρόθεν τῶν [from wax])"}, {"id": "krino-quote3", "translation": "I judge abundant wealth"}, {"id": "krino-quote4", "translation": "judge the reverence due to the gods"}, {"id": "krino-quote5", "translation": "and Ares will decide the work with dice"}, {"id": "krino-quote6", "translation": "and it is hard to decide"}, {"id": "krino-quote7", "translation": "I judge you to be victorious"}, {"id": "krino-quote8", "translation": "and judge a straight justice"}, {"id": "krino-quote9", "translation": "judge the case"}, {"id": "krino-quote10", "translation": "whether justly or not, judge this blood according to your own mind"}, {"id": "krino-quote11", "translation": "judging first cases of shed blood"}, {"id": "krino-quote12", "translation": "this is my task, to judge the final case"}, {"id": "krino-quote13", "translation": "how will the contest be decided?"}, {"id": "krino-quote14", "translation": "even if the vote is equal"}, {"id": "krino-quote15", "translation": "and I first judged from dreams what must come to pass in waking"}, {"id": "krino-quote16", "translation": "and we judge that all these things will turn out well for you"}, {"id": "krino-quote17", "translation": "but you judged these things too lightly"}, {"id": "krino-quote18", "translation": "and I judge him so as to hold together"}, {"id": "krisis-orth1", "translation": "judgment, decision"}, {"id": "krisis-def1", "translation": "judgment, decision"}, {"id": "krisis-quote1", "translation": "thus they depart in the judgment of the gods"}, {"id": "krites-orth1", "translation": "judge"}, {"id": "krites-def1", "translation": "judge"}, {"id": "krites-note1", "translation": "about an interpreter of dreams."}, {"id": "krites-quote1", "translation": "do not choose me as judge"}, {"id": "krites-quote2", "translation": "kindly indeed is the first judge of these dreams"}, {"id": "krokobaptos-orth1", "translation": "dyed with saffron"}, {"id": "krokobaptos-def1", "translation": "dyed with saffron"}, {"id": "krokobaptos-quote1", "translation": "lifting a saffron-dyed shoe of the foot"}, {"id": "krokobaphes-orth1", "translation": "saffron-colored"}, {"id": "krokobaphes-def1", "translation": "saffron-colored"}]}